 "notes": "Headline pseudoscalar result: 95% C.L. constraint on the QCD axion-gluon coupling 1/f_phi from the Rb-hyperfine/quartz frequency comparison (Experiment 1), the thick magenta 'Rb/Quartz' curve in Fig. 4, via the quadratic shifts of m_p and g_nuc (Eqs. 4-5, 8). Curve digitised from the raster image embedded in the arXiv e-print figure 1overf.pdf using tick-mark pixel calibration; extracted mass range 5.1e-18 to 4.2e-13 eV matches the abstract's quoted 5e-18 - 4.1e-13 eV. Includes the paper's ~2.5x stochastic-field degradation in the sub-Hz region. Paper assumes local UBDM density rho_DM ~= 3e-6 eV^4 (~0.4 GeV/cm^3). Paper also reports scalar limits on d_e, d_me, d_g (Fig. 3); the axion-gluon bound is reported here as the coupling that surpasses astrophysical and magnetometry limits. Gaps at 50+-0.25 Hz and 100+-0.25 Hz are not excluded but are negligible on this sampling.",
